摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Delegate from OpenClaw, Pi or DeepSeek Harness to existing Codex CLI, Codex Desktop and Claude Code sessions. Track progress and results.","id":"gh:1240150958","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"agent-knock-knock","slug":"scotthuang/agent-knock-knock","topics":["agent-orchestration","claude-code","codex","coding-agents","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh-plugin","herdr","human-in-the-loop","local-first","openclaw","openclaw-plugin","terminal-control","terminal-handoff","tmux","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Delegate from OpenClaw, Pi or DeepSeek Harness to existing Codex CLI, Codex Desktop and Claude Code "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"sessions. Track progress and results."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Agent Knock Knock (AKK)"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Agent Knock Knock lets **OpenClaw** control your existing **Codex CLI, Codex Desktop, and Claude Cod"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"e** conversations. Watch work without staring at a terminal, send the next instruction from chat, an"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"d get callbacks when the coding agent finishes or needs attention."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"AKK never launches a hidden replacement agent. The controller Host, the human, and AKK all use the s"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ame visible conversation and native coding-agent session."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Stay in the terminal. Stay in control. No hooks. No agent-side plugins. No YOLO.**"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"*Codex CLI 0.159 and later support direct control. For earlier versions, use tmux or Herdr.*"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## What AKK Gives You"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"AKK 0.14.0 introduces Codex CLI shared-backend control, Codex Desktop support, and exact-task recove"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ry. Desktop includes discovery, task sending, Status, and exact task Watches. List follows saved Des"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ktop sidebar membership and keeps unconnected entries visible; open a conversation in Desktop before"},{"id":"p8s4","text":" sending to it. Desktop supports command/file approval decisions, blocking and asynchronous answers,"},{"id":"p8s5","text":" per-conversation permissions, explicit model and Plan/default settings, and exact task cancellation"},{"id":"p8s6","text":". See Desktop compatibility and usage."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Codex CLI sessions connected to a shared backend can also be controlled directly, without tmux or He"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"rdr. Native CLI rows support task sending, exact Watch and callbacks, command/file approvals, blocki"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ng and asynchronous answers, and per-thread permission settings. See the CLI shared-backend guide."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"AKK provides Claude Code direct control: discover an already-open CLI, send tasks, read progress, an"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"d receive completion callbacks without tmux/Herdr, Claude plugins, or hooks. Standard `claude` and c"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"onfigured wrappers such as `tclaude` use the same adapter; no wrapper is required. Live observations"},{"id":"p10s4","text":" include Claude Code `2.1.295` and `2.1.296` on macOS, not a minimum-version requirement. The native"},{"id":"p10s5","text":" connection requires Python 3 on the AKK side."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Starting with AKK 0.15.0, new Claude Code sends automatically prefer a managed Turn through an exact"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" controllable tmux/Herdr terminal, so supported approvals follow the returned `turn_id`. Without tha"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"t terminal, AKK uses the native inbox and returns a Watch with completion and notify-only waiting ca"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"llbacks. Existing task receipts keep their original route; native Watches do not gain approval autho"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"rity when a terminal later becomes available. Codex CLI continues to prefer its shared backend."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The existing terminal workflows remain available for Codex or Claude Code running in tmux or Herdr:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Codex CLI 0.158.0/0.159.0/0.159.2/0.159.3/0.160.0/0.162.1/0.164.0/0.165.0/0.166.0/0.167.0 supports e"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"xact paginated task Watches for ordinary terminal\nSend, native question responses, and durable compl"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"etion callbacks. The adapter\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## How It Works"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"For Codex CLI, AKK prefers the shared backend when it verifies the exact live conversation. You sele"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ct a conversation and an action; AKK selects the connection. Before dispatch, an unavailable backend"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" or unsupported operation may use a verified terminal route. Busy, blocked, or uncertain results do "},{"id":"p16s4","text":"not trigger a retry through another connection."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Codex CLI shared-backend connections and Codex Desktop work without tmux or Herdr\nwhen the condition"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"s below are met. Older CLI setups without a direct connection\ncan use a supported terminal route. Cl"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"aude Code direct control is available under the separate boundary below."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Component | Supported boundary |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Terminal hosts | tmux; local Herdr with per-operation capability checks (AKK `0.14.15`+). Tested H"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"erdr baselines: `0.8.0` / protocol `19` and `0.9.5` / protocol `22`. See the Herdr guide. |\n| Codex "},{"id":"p21s3","text":"Desktop | macOS with a compatible live connection; app updates alone do not disable controls. See th"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"e tested versions and operation matrix. |\n| Codex CLI shared backend | Live-tested on macOS: CLI/bac"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"kend `0.167.0` in the 0.16.12 review, `0.166.0` in the 0.16.11 review, `0.165.0` in the 0.16.4 revie"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"w, `0.164.0` in the 0.14.17 review, `0.162.1` + `0.162.1`, and previously `0.160.0` + `0.162.0`. Req"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"uires a loaded main CLI conversation and compatible live protocol. These are tested combinations, **"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"not a numeric minimum**. |\n| Claude Code direct connection | macOS, compatible native peer protocol "},{"id":"p21s9","text":"`1`, and Python 3 available to AKK. Live observations include `2.1.295` and `2.1.296`; these are not"},{"id":"p21s10","text":" minimum versions. Standard `claude` and configured wrappers use the same adapter. See the direct gu"},{"id":"p21s11","text":"ide for task and interaction boundaries. |\n| Terminal coding agents | Reviewed Codex profiles includ"},{"id":"p21s12","text":"e `0.160.0`, `0.162.1`, `0.164.0`, `0.165.0`, `0.166.0` and `0.167.0`; Claude fixtures include `2.1."},{"id":"p21s13","text":"285`, with live observations on `2.1.295`/`2.1.296`. An otherwise eligible, complete `x.y.z` Claude "},{"id":"p21s14","text":"version may attempt supported controls through runtime validation even without an exact regression p"},{"id":"p21s15","text":"rofile. Actual identity, protocol and UI evidence determine availability; unknown dialogs are not gu"},{"id":"p21s16","text":"essed. |\n| OpenClaw | `2026.6.5`+; plugin API and Gateway `2026.5.12`+ |\n| Pi connector | Pi `1.2.0`"},{"id":"p21s17","text":" and `0.84.4`; connector `0.1.0-poc.20` (`next`), pinned AKK `0.16.12` |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Security and Privacy"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"AKK controls local coding-agent sessions, so treat installation as privileged local automation. Use "},{"id":"p23s2","text":"an unprivileged OS account, restrict backend, tmux, Herdr, and Desktop IPC sockets, keep the state d"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"irectory private, and review approval prompts before allowing input. Ordinary AKK Send does not chan"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"ge agent permissions or require YOLO mode. Desktop tasks inherit that conversation's current setting"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"s. Respond to supported approvals and questions through their advertised actions; unknown request fo"},{"id":"p23s6","text":"rms remain manual. The explicit Codex permission tool applies only the user-selected native mode; mo"},{"id":"p23s7","text":"del-facing tools never receive terminal-control tokens, callback credentials, Composer text, or appr"},{"id":"p23s8","text":"ever receive terminal-control tokens, callback credentials, Composer text, or approval fingerprints."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Report vulnerabilities privately using GitHub Security Advisories. Please do not include secrets, pr"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ivate terminal output, or credentials in a public issue."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
